# Preserve All Existing Trip Data and Photos

This app stores irreplaceable family memories. Shared trip data and gallery
photos/videos live in **Netlify Blobs** (stores `karens-gallery` and the trip
data store used by `trip.mts`) on the production site (staudachers.netlify.app).

## Hard rules

- **Never delete, overwrite, or truncate existing blobs** in the gallery or
  trip stores. Do not call `store.delete(...)`, re-`set` an existing key with
  new content, or wipe/recreate a store — unless the user explicitly asks to
  delete a *specific* item.
- **Never rename the blob stores** (`karens-gallery`, trip store). Renaming
  orphans all existing data. If a new store is truly needed, migrate by
  *copying* data over and confirm the copy before pointing code at it.
- **Uploads must only add new keys.** Generate unique filenames (the existing
  `Date.now()-random` pattern); never reuse an existing key.
- **API changes must stay backward compatible with stored data.** Old image
  URLs (`/api/gallery/images/<name>`) and existing trip JSON must keep
  working after any refactor.
- **Testing must not touch production storage.** Test uploads/changes against
  local storage (`netlify dev` local blobs) — never against the live site's
  stores.
- **Bulk cleanup, "reset", or "start fresh" operations are forbidden** even if
  they would simplify a fix. Ask the user first and get explicit confirmation
  listing exactly what would be removed.

## Examples

```ts
// ❌ BAD — wipes shared photos
const { blobs } = await store.list();
for (const b of blobs) await store.delete(b.key);

// ❌ BAD — overwrites existing trip data wholesale during a "migration"
await tripStore.set('trip', JSON.stringify(newDefaultData));

// ✅ GOOD — additive only; existing keys untouched
const name = `${Date.now()}-${Math.random().toString(36).slice(2, 10)}.jpg`;
await store.set(name, bytes);
```
